+# Published steel-data scope and conditional ratio test
+
+Prior inspection found exactly 756 data rows, 22 columns, and 22 attribute definitions: 688 rows labelled Literature and 68 This study. These are source-labelled rows, not 756 recovered pieces or independent physical observations. No selected W14A/B,C12a/b,M4/M14/M10a/b ID match was found by the previously described exact-field and hyphen/whitespace-insensitive lookup. All source strings remain preserved.
+
+Before further arithmetic: record counts and unique specimen/sample strings by Source, not by assumed origin; enumerate missing fields without treating NA as zero. Preserve Year, T, normalization criteria, units and publication-date descriptions by source. The T field is documented as tensile test temperature; it is not a historical 2001 exposure measurement. Year has source-dependent meaning and is not automatically the test year. The nine This study specimen strings do not, without intake/source joins, establish nine recovered building columns.
+
+Check the possible 0.2%-offset normalization relation RFy = FY002/FY20 only for finite numeric fields and nonzero denominator, recording all original inputs, recalculated value, signed residual and maximum/median absolute residual separately for Literature and This study. Report scope and every exclusion; do not select a preferred source value, replace original data, declare an undocumented tolerance passed, or treat an arithmetic residual as proof of faulty science. Actual normalization/baseline/rounding and version rules remain inputs. The separate 2%-total-elongation RFy02/FY02 fields must not be checked against a 0.2%-offset room-temperature denominator without a supported matching-baseline rule.
+
+Read the actual bibliography's cover/method and variable/source-reference pages visually. Compare the manifest's 2011 last-updated label with the bibliography's March5,2018 date and its 2016 augmentation description without silently dating the CSV or adjudicating the field meanings. The source is a published summary, not native instrument curves, furnace controls, calibration, custody, a 2005 delivery copy or W14B administrative disposition. Follow no further report/data downloads in this unit.
