+# Exact remaining inputs and disconfirming checks
+
+1. The actual DOC-NIST-2013-001311 request, substantive disposition and attachments. The acquired 2013 log and separate 2014-000573 response do not supply them.
+2. Actual W14A/B and related intake, marking, alias, building/region-attribution, field/coupon transfer and retention records and native workbook history.
+3. For the CSV rows at issue, the exact normalization worksheet, baseline coupon/series IDs, denominator-selection and rounding/aggregation rules, original machine curves, furnace/strain/calibration and processing records. Test whether FY20 is intended as each row's RFy denominator before assigning an error.
+4. Native/earlier dataset editions and the TN1714/TN1907 figure/row crosswalk, with release or revision manifests. Compare all original tuples; do not repair source fields to make ratios agree.
+5. Source-specific 0.2%-offset versus 2%-total-elongation definitions and matched room-temperature baselines before extending the calculation to RFy02.
+6. Original FAA correction/receipt and signed disposition; telephone carrier/operator/recipient/schema/clock joins; recorder configuration/custody/clock and materials raw/specimen/calibration requirements remain open with their existing owners.
+
+An applicable baseline or source transformation could weaken the apparent discrepancy; a documented erroneous denominator or unsupported transcription could strengthen it. Neither is established here. No original curve or administrative outcome was acquired by retrieving this summary dataset. No request, contact, fee or physical experiment is performed or authorized by this list.
